{% comment %}
  The product's price, on its own row.

  Every other place a number appears in this buy box hangs off a selling plan —
  the supply cards, the purchase plan cards, the simple offer. A product that
  carries no plans therefore renders a buy box with no price in it at all, which
  is the gap this block fills. It quotes the variant itself, so it is correct on
  a plain product and needs nothing configured to be right.

  On a product that DOES carry plans it still belongs, and follows the live
  selection rather than contradicting it: the script mirrors the selected card's
  own price and compare-at into this row, and falls back to the variant's when
  no card is selected. So the row always says what the Add To Cart button is
  about to charge.

  Savings are read off the variant payload rather than subtracted here at
  runtime, because those numbers arrive already formatted as money — see the
  section's variant payload.

  Accepts:
  - block {Object} - the price_display block. Reads settings.savings_display,
    settings.save_label, settings.show_compare, settings.show_dividers.
  - current_variant {Object} - variant whose price is quoted; blank in preview.

  Usage:
  {% render 'CWC_pdp-price-display__block',
    block: block,
    current_variant: current_variant
  %}
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign savings_display = block.settings.savings_display | default: 'percent'
  assign show_compare = block.settings.show_compare
  assign save_label = block.settings.save_label | default: 'Save'

  assign price = current_variant.price
  assign compare_price = current_variant.compare_at_price

  comment
    "On sale" is the one condition the whole row keys off: no compare-at, or one
    that is not actually higher, means no strikeout and no badge — a "Save $0"
    chip beside a full-price product reads as a broken discount.
  endcomment
  assign on_sale = false
  if compare_price > price
    assign on_sale = true
  endif

  assign save_amount = compare_price | minus: price
  comment
    100.0, not 100: divided_by on two integers truncates, so the round
    below never sees the fraction and a 30% saving reads as 29%.
  endcomment
  assign save_percent = save_amount | times: 100.0 | divided_by: compare_price | round
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  Rendered even with no product bound, so the theme editor shows the row where
  it will sit instead of a gap the merchant has to guess at. The placeholder
  numbers never reach a shopper — a live product always resolves a variant.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div
  class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__price{% if block.settings.show_dividers %} cwc_product-hero-buy-box__price--divided{% endif %}"
  data-cwc-price-display
  {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
>
  <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__price-current" data-cwc-price-current>
    {%- if current_variant != blank -%}
      {{- price | money -}}
    {%- else -%}
      {{- 4900 | money -}}
    {%- endif -%}
  </span>

  {%- comment -%}
    Both the strikeout and the badge are always in the DOM, hidden rather than
    omitted when the variant is not on sale. The script only ever flips their
    display, so a size change from a full-price variant to a discounted one can
    bring them back — markup that was never rendered could not be revived.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if show_compare -%}
    <span
      class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__price-compare"
      data-cwc-price-compare
      {% unless on_sale %}style="display: none;"{% endunless %}
    >
      {%- if on_sale -%}{{ compare_price | money }}{%- endif -%}
    </span>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- if savings_display != 'none' -%}
    <span
      class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__price-save"
      data-cwc-price-save
      data-cwc-price-save-mode="{{ savings_display }}"
      {% unless on_sale %}style="display: none;"{% endunless %}
    >
      {%- if save_label != blank -%}
        <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__price-save-label">{{ save_label }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
      <span class="cwc_product-hero-buy-box__price-save-amount" data-cwc-price-save-amount>
        {%- if on_sale -%}
          {%- if savings_display == 'dollar' -%}
            {{- save_amount | money_without_trailing_zeros -}}
          {%- else -%}
            {{- save_percent }}%
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </span>
    </span>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>
